OL,3,GNEWSANurses speak out against rising
OL,4,Atide of abuse
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo nurses have said the abuse they are
OL,7,Ffacing from patients, which has
OL,8,Fincluded shouting and having objects
OL,9,Fthrown at them, is getting worse.
OL,11,FWashington community nurses Shannon
OL,12,FMalloy and Lydia Taylor said verbal
OL,13,Fattacks from patients had "massively"
OL,14,Fincreased in the last five years.
OL,16,FTaylor said the issue had become so bad
OL,17,Fshe sometimes dreaded going into work
OL,18,Fand had considered leaving nursing. She
OL,19,Fsaid she feared the abuse experienced
OL,20,Fby staff would only continue to worsen.
